Hi [~accountid:712020:0da4d322-db80-449c-9041-1b580c533aa4]

Thanks for the request. Just to remind that per our internal rules, Bolt may only agree to custom templates with business customers:

* if the estimated number of monthly rides is above 1000
* if the customer is deemed “exceptional” by the regional sales manager;

----

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
As for the template, unfortunately, we cannot accept the suggested Data Processing Agreement as its concept is contrary to our operational model - we never accept them. Please respond with the following:
{panel}

{quote}_Dear [_]_

_We regret to inform you that we cannot accept the suggested Data Processing Agreement and a controller-to-processor relationship, as this contradicts our operational model with business customers._

_As an online platform, Bolt operates solely as an independent data controller when serving our business customers, with no exceptions. This relationship is consistently governed by Section 4 of our Bolt Business Terms and Conditions, and we do not enter into agreements that modify this established model. Our approach ensures full compliance with Kenyan data protection law._

_We trust this explanation clarifies our position. Thank you for your understanding._{quote}

----

{panel:bgColor=#eae6ff}
IF the customer fulfils the conditions above to be eligible for a custom agreement, and also does not accept our push back and still wants to sign a DPA, we can suggest a custom data sharing template.
{panel}

