{panel:bgColor=#e3fcef}
*Privacy Statement for the Request for Information (RFI)* - this is ok and can remain. This document serves as a transparency statement, outlining how Huawei will handle the personal data of Bolt’s personnel. It does not dictate our personal data transfer arrangements.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
As a general reminder, it is important that our data transfer obligations between the parties remain governed by Section 4 of the BB T&Cs, which is our standard practice.

Please inform me if there are any changes to this section or if Huawei raises any questions related to personal data protection.
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Summary of the case*
{panel}

* On April 3, 2025, the Cybercrime Division of the Ministry of Internal Affairs received a statement from Davit Kodanashvili, Head of the Legal Support Unit at the Security Department of JSC Bank of Georgia. 
* According to the statement, since the end of 2024, *there has been a significant increase in the number of customer complaints submitted to Bank of Georgia.* These complaints concern unauthorized orders allegedly placed through Glovo (Glovoapp Georgia LLC, ID 402099475,), Bolt (BOLT OPERATIONS OU, ID 14532901), and Wolt (Wolt Georgia LLC, ID 405260042, Tax Code 133023880). *Customers claim they did not make these orders and that funds were fraudulently withdrawn from their bank accounts based on these transactions.*
* According to the statement, it appears that Glovo, Wolt, and Bolt *do not require cardholders to enter a verification code sent via SMS to confirm the linking of a bank card.* Instead, they verify the card’s validity by charging and immediately refunding 1 GEL from the linked account. While this transaction does not appear in the account statement, the cardholder does receive a corresponding SMS notification.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Assumption made by the regulators*
{panel}

* The statement also notes that the above-mentioned companies *have declared they accept the risks associated with unauthorized withdrawals* made through their platforms and *compensate customers for any resulting losses.*
* From Davit Kodanashvili’s statement, it is clear that he has a reasonable suspicion that a c*ertain group is involved in registering user accounts with these companies and then linking bank cards—issued to other individuals—to those accounts.*

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Data requested*
{panel}

* Identity data of the account holders (users) 
