Hello, [~accountid:628b90a588ebba006f94b43c].

Checking both sides of ID documents is a usual practice and is encouraged due to the following legal and practical reasons:

# Back side often contains additional security features, barcode, etc., and sometimes issuing authority or expiry details. Verifying both sides ensures that all information is visible and can be authenticated;
# Many fake IDs only replicate the front side. Reviewing the back side as well helps detecting forged documents by checking for tampered or missing features (e.g., holograms, etc.);
# When storing digital copies of identity documents, full records (both sides) are often needed for completeness and traceability during audits or reviews. 

Please note that even though the Digital Service Act does not explicitly require collecting both sides of ID documents (see Article 30 thereof), it is highly recommended doing so in order to:

* fully verify the document’s authenticity.
* detect fraud or inconsistencies;
* ensure complete and thorough due diligence.

